  "note": "Election of the Coleraine Borough Council, 21 May 1958: four aldermen and twelve councillors returned unopposed after one withdrawal (Belfast News-Letter, 8 and 9 May 1958). Thirteen nominations were received for twelve councillorships; Mr. Leonard E. Trautner then withdrew, so there was no contest. The first eight names listed were retiring members. Aldermen Sutherland, N. F. Christie, Patterson and Tosh did not seek re-election. No party label was printed. Returned unopposed.",
  "correctionNote": "Corrected from the page image of the Belfast News-Letter, 8 May 1958, p. 6 (council-audit, Nov 2026): the nominations list that names the twelve members is now cited (the 9 May page reports only Trautner's withdrawal); Name_As_Printed 'J. M'Kee' as printed (was 'J. McKee')."
